Z||000004||Kwez||11-23-2001||10:12 PM||||for info on the 4.9 swap : <A HREF="http://members.fortunecity.com/bubbajoexx/" TARGET=_blank>http://members.fortunecity.com/bubbajoexx/</A> <BR>& <A HREF="http://communities.msn.ca/FieroCaddySwapGroup/messageboard.msnw" TARGET=_blank>http://communities.msn.ca/FieroCaddySwapGroup/messageboard.msnw</A> <P>$400 for a brand new Aurora V8 ??<BR>"she-it". ( =&gt; <A HREF="http://compositeeti.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://compositeeti.com/</A>  )<BR><B><I>I</I></B> would look into it at that price. <P>It might mean more 'do it yourself' stuff, but there's more & more info / experience on the N* swap now.<P>(as KMSSFiero said, Aurora V8 is supposed to be same engine w. smaller displacement. But I'm just repeating info I heard before)<P>also see : <A HREF="http://compositeeti.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://compositeeti.com/</A> <P>keep us posted !<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Kwez (edited 11-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||westtexas||11-23-2001||10:48 PM||||Jeff, I have thoroughly enjoyed the threads you've started and learned a lot. The recent wheel one was great. I spent the last hour looking through tirerack.com. That said, your statement about whether to use an <BR>Aurora V8 or a 4.9 shows a lot of inexperience. I'm inexperienced. There is no choice for either of us but the 4.9. The aurora will scream, will frighten the natives, will suck asphalt off the road. But can you pull it off when you ask "which one would be easier to make run(ecm)?" Like I said, I haven't been down either road. But have you perhaps noticed the Northstar folks talking about serious cradle mods. Have you actually pulled a Fiero cradle yet? You need to start simple with a 4.9. It fits the cradle. Ed Parks is going to have the 4.9 fuel injection figured out. You have several choices of transmissions. You would be following a beaten path. How many Aurora swaps are you aware of? My advice is do the easy one first. Enjoy it and then decide if need the Aurora. Great ideas are necessary but success lies in the details. There are fewer details in the 4.9.<P>Good luck,<BR>Robert<p>[This message has been edited by westtexas (edited 11-23-2001).]||||reg||1
